  "notes": "West leads the ♠10 against 6NT. It appears that South will have to guess diamonds after finding out that clubs split 4-1. If East is the defender with 4 clubs, South can squeeze East into guessing diamonds for him.\n\nAfter winning the spade opening lead, South should test clubs with the ♣K and ♣Q. If East turns up with 4 clubs South runs the spades followed by the hearts. On the last heart East must come down to a singleton diamond. South discards a club and leads a diamond from the dummy.\n\nIf East started with either the ♦A or the ♦Q, he will be forced to play it. South will be able to develop his twelfth trick in diamonds.",
